---
import { alternatesFor } from '../../lib/statiske-alternates';
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  lang="en"
  tittel="Privacy policy"
  beskrivelse="Read the Dream Guide's privacy policy. What data we collect, why, and what rights you have under GDPR."
  alternates={alternatesFor('personvern')}
>
  <div class="static-page">
    <span class="static-label">Legal</span>
    <h1 class="static-title">Privacy policy</h1>

    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lead">
        The Dream Guide collects a minimum of anonymized data to understand
        how the site is used and to show advertising. We never sell
        information about you, and you can withdraw your consent at any
        time.
      </p>

      <p><em>Last updated: June 1, 2026</em></p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        The Dream Guide (drommeguiden.no) is a website providing information
        about dream symbols and dream interpretation. The site is owned and
        operated by Herman Gautefall Olsson, who acts as the data controller
        under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).
      </p>

      <h2>What data we collect</h2>
      <p>
        We do not collect data that directly identifies you (name, phone
        number or email address) unless you choose to contact us yourself.
        The data typically collected automatically when you visit the site
        is:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>IP address (anonymized/masked before it is stored)</li>
        <li>Which pages you visit, for how long, and in what order</li>
        <li>Clicks and scroll depth on individual pages</li>
        <li>Browser, operating system and approximate geographic area (country/region)</li>
        <li>Referral source (which page or search engine you arrived from)</li>
        <li>Operational data from Cloudflare needed to deliver the site and protect it against abuse</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Services we use</h2>
      <p>We rely on a small number of third-party services to run, analyze and fund the site:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> — anonymized analysis of site
          usage. Measures how many people visit which pages, how long they
          stay and where they come from. IP addresses are masked before
          being stored, and the data is used only in aggregate to improve
          our content.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Cloudflare</strong> — operationally necessary
          infrastructure for CDN delivery, DDoS protection and security.
          Processes technical data such as IP address and request headers
          in order to deliver the site quickly and safely.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Google AdSense</strong> — we show ads on article pages to
          fund the operation of the Dream Guide. If you give consent, Google
          may show personalized ads based on your interests; without
          consent, only general, non-personalized ads are shown. Google
          then sets cookies such as <code>_gads</code>, <code>IDE</code>,
          <code>NID</code> and <code>__gpi</code> to deliver, measure and
          limit the display of ads. See our
          <a href="/en/cookies/">cookie policy</a> for an overview.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Legal basis</h2>
      <p>Our processing of your data is based on the following grounds under GDPR:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Consent (Art. 6(1)(a)):</strong> for analytics (Google
          Analytics 4) and advertising (Google AdSense). You give consent
          via the consent banner the first time you visit the site, and can
          withdraw it at any time.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f)):</strong> for
          operationally necessary functions such as CDN delivery, DDoS
          protection and basic security logging via Cloudflare. These
          cannot be turned off without the site ceasing to function.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Your rights under GDPR</h2>
      <p>Under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) you have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Access</strong> — request a copy of the data we hold about you</li>
        <li><strong>Rectification</strong> — require that inaccurate data be corrected</li>
        <li><strong>Erasure</strong> — require that your data be deleted (the "right to be forgotten")</li>
        <li><strong>Data portability</strong> — receive your data in a machine-readable format</li>
        <li><strong>Object</strong> — object to processing based on legitimate interest</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Complain</strong> to
          <a href="https://www.datatilsynet.no" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the Norwegian Data Protection Authority (Datatilsynet)</a>
          if you believe we are processing your data in violation of the
          rules
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How to withdraw consent</h2>
      <p>
        Once our consent solution is in place, you will find a link labeled
        <strong>"Cookie settings"</strong> in the footer on every page.
        There you can change your consent for analytics and advertising at
        any time, or withdraw it entirely. Changes take effect immediately.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can also block or delete cookies through your browser's own
        settings. See the <a href="/en/cookies/">cookie policy</a> for
        concrete steps.
      </p>

      <h2>More about advertising</h2>
      <p>
        Ads on the Dream Guide are delivered through Google AdSense. How
        Google uses data in connection with advertising is described in
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's advertising policy</a>.
        You can also control what kind of ads are shown to you across
        Google's services via
        <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">adssettings.google.com</a>,
        independent of your consent on this site.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .static-page {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .static-label {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-nav);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 1.5px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .static-title {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 36px;
    color: var(--color-text-heading);
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    font-weight: 400;
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .static-title { font-size: 44px; }
  }
  .prose .lead {
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-text-body);
    padding: 18px 20px;
    background: rgba(123, 111, 160, 0.05);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-primary);
    border-radius: 0 12px 12px 0;
    margin: 0 0 24px;
  }
  .prose code {
    font-family: ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.92em;
    padding: 1px 6px;
    background: rgba(123, 111, 160, 0.08);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }
</style>
